{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (#5602) that requires implementing `cmd/test/main.go` - a Go reimplementation of the POSIX `test` (aka `[`) command. The task scope covers only SRD104 requirements R1.1 (file test operators), R1.2 (file comparison operators), R2.1 (string operators), and R2.2 (integer comparison operators). The code must be structured to support future addition of R3.x (logical operators like !, -a, -o, parentheses) and R4.x (exit codes, SIGPIPE) without restructuring. The SIGPIPE handler must be installed per design decision D1 even though R4.2 isn't formally in scope.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - POSIX `test` command implementation in Go\n   - File test operators: -e, -f, -d, -s, -r, -w, -x, -L/-h, -b, -c, -p, -S, -g, -u, -k, -G, -O, -t FD\n   - File comparison operators: -nt (newer than), -ot (older than), -ef (same device+inode)\n   - String operators: -z (zero length), -n (non-zero length), = (equal), != (not equal), STRING (non-empty)\n   - Integer comparison operators: -eq, -ne, -lt, -le, -gt, -ge\n   - Non-goals: No == operator (use =), no regex matching (=~)\n   - Differential testing pattern against `gtest` (GNU coreutils reference binary)\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Go module: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`\n   - Execution constitution: 40-line function limit (E8), 500-line file limit (E9), DRY (E10)\n   - Exit codes: 0 (true), 1 (false), 2 (syntax error)\n   - Copyright header: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd104-test.yaml` (READ)\n      - This is the SRD defining all requirements for the test utility\n      - Key requirements in scope: R1.1 (file tests), R1.2 (file comparisons), R2.1 (string tests), R2.2 (integer comparisons)\n      - Non-goals: no == operator, no regex matching (=~)\n      - Full content read and captured above in conversation\n   \n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (PROVIDED INLINE)\n      - Shows the InstallSIGPIPEHandler pattern to follow\n      ```go\n      func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n          c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n          signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n          go func() {\n              <-c\n              os.Exit(0)\n          }()\n      }\n      ```\n   \n   - `cmd/test/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n      - The main file to implement - evaluates conditional expressions\n      - Must support all file test, file comparison, string, and integer operators\n      - Must call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at start of main\n      - Must be structured for future extensibility (R3.x logical operators, R4.x exit codes)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - implementation has not started.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read and analyzed the SRD to understand all requirements in scope\n   - No code written yet; interrupted before implementation began\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The massive task prompt containing the full stitch task specification including: role definition, repository_files list, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source_code, requirement_states), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task description with requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, shared_protocols, package_contracts, and constraints.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Request for a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/test/main.go` implementing R1.1, R1.2, R2.1, R2.2\n   - Verify compilation: `go build -o bin/test ./cmd/test/`\n   - Verify: `go vet ./cmd/test/...`\n   - Ensure code structure supports future R3.x and R4.x requirements\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file (`srd104-test.yaml`) and was about to plan and implement `cmd/test/main.go`. No code has been written yet. The implementation needs to:\n   \n   - Start with copyright header and package main\n   - Import `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys` for SIGPIPE\n   - Import `os`, `strconv`, `fmt`, `syscall` for file operations and integer parsing\n   - Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at top of main\n   - Parse arguments and evaluate conditional expressions\n   - Implement file test unary operators (-e, -f, -d, -s, -r, -w, -x, -L/-h, -b, -c, -p, -S, -g, -u, -k, -G, -O, -t)\n   - Implement file comparison binary operators (-nt, -ot, -ef)\n   - Implement string unary operators (-z, -n) and binary operators (=, !=)\n   - Implement integer comparison binary operators (-eq, -ne, -lt, -le, -gt, -ge)\n   - Exit 0 for true, 1 for false, 2 for errors\n   - Keep functions under 40 lines, use strategy pattern for extensibility\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/test/main.go` implementing all four requirements (R1.1, R1.2, R2.1, R2.2) following the task description: \"Implement srd104-test requirement R1.1, R1.2, R2.1, R2.2 as specified in the SRD.\" The implementation should be structured per D4: \"Structure the implementation so requirements R3.1, R3.2, R4.1, R4.2 can be added in a follow-up task without restructuring existing code.\" After writing the file, verify with `go build -o bin/test ./cmd/test/` and `go vet ./cmd/test/...`.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5602/8480b89f-18fc-4679-98ec-87305aa69d35.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any furth